From: Ayushman Chhabra <14110965+ayushmanchhabra@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 20:59:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Generate the resized window icon's representations up front

window.icon images larger than 128px are resized lazily, so the icon has
no representations until one is requested. Wayland's XdgToplevel::SetIcon
only sends the ones that exist, so the window got an empty icon and showed
the default one.

Refs: nwjs/nw.js#8397
---
 src/browser/nw_extensions_browser_hooks.cc | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/browser/nw_extensions_browser_hooks.cc b/src/browser/nw_extensions_browser_hooks.cc
index a330ec3..0dcb25d 100644
--- a/src/browser/nw_extensions_browser_hooks.cc
+++ b/src/browser/nw_extensions_browser_hooks.cc
@@ -285,6 +285,10 @@ void LoadNWAppAsExtensionHook(base::DictValue* manifest,
           gfx::ImageSkiaOperations::CreateResizedImage(*originImageSkia,
                                                        skia::ImageOperations::RESIZE_GOOD,
                                                        gfx::Size(128, 128));
+        // The resized image is generated lazily, and some consumers only
+        // read the representations it already has (e.g. the Wayland window
+        // icon), so generate them now.
+        resizedImageSkia.EnsureRepsForSupportedScales();
         app_icon = gfx::Image(resizedImageSkia);
       }
       SetAppIcon(app_icon);
